    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1030">

                <pb facs="1287" n="1273" sameAs="frus:frus1945v09/pg1273"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">819.011/9–1945: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Panama</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Donnelly</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Panamá</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-09-19T11:00:00-05:00">September 19,
                            1945—11 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 3:09 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>851. The committee studying proposed constitution will vote today on articles
                    relating to nationalization of commerce. While proposed compromise represents a
                    substantial improvement over original draft, the President has again informed me
                    that he still feels that nationalization of commerce should take the form of
                    separate legislation and <pb facs="1288" n="1274" xml:id="pg1274"/> that he will
                    use his influence in this direction at the appropriate time.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Donnelly</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
